<title>USA: U.S. Mar single-family home sales fell 2.5 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Mar single-family home sales fell 2.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department reported sales of new single-family homes, seasonally adjusted, with percent changes from prior month (numbers in 1,000s).</p>
<p> -		 Pct--Mar    Feb-(Prev)    Jan-(Prev)</p>
<p> Total Units  -2.5  813    834   811     825   817</p>
<p> -By Region:   Pct--Mar    Feb-(Prev)    Jan-(Prev)</p>
<p> - Northeast -16.1   94    112    95     111   107</p>
<p> - Midwest     2.5  123    120   141     137   146</p>
<p> - South     -10.5  351    392   364     380   377</p>
<p> - West	 17.7  246    209   210     198   188</p>
<p>Total March sales of single-family homes rose 14.3 percent from an annualized rate of 711,000 units a year ago.</p>
<p>    In 1,000s:	Mar     Feb--(Prev)    Jan--(Prev)</p>
<p> Actual Units Sold   78	70     67	61     60</p>
<p>Sales Prices:</p>
<p> --Mean	     171.5   169.9  174.5   171.1  170.2</p>
<p> --Median	   142.5   141.0  143.2   145.0  143.8</p>
<p>Note-Actual number of new single-family units sold is not seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists forecast March single-family home sales at a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 794,000 units.  </p>
<p>The department also revised monthly percent changes of total sales, seasonally adjusted, from prior months as follows:</p>
<p>    -	     Feb-(Prev)   Jan-(Prev)   Dec--(Prev)</p>
<p> Total Units    1.1  -0.7    3.9   3.5    0.8    0.1</p>
<p>The annualized sales rate for December was revised to 794,000 units from 789,000.</p>
<p> Number of Months:     Mar    Feb-(Prev)   Jan-(Prev)</p>
<p> -Supply of Homes	4.5    4.4   4.6    4.7   4.8</p>
<p> 1,000 Units:	    Mar    Feb-(Prev)   Jan-(Prev)</p>
<p> -End-Month Inventory  297    307   312    314   316</p>
<p>The March end-of-month inventory was the lowest since April 1994 when it was also 297,000 units, the department said.</p>
<p>The February revised annualized home sales rate of 834,000 units was the strongest since April 1986 when it was 857,000 units, the department said.</p>
<p>The West's home sales rate of 246,000 units was the strongest since November 1993 when it was 262,000 units, it said.</p>
</text>
